{"id": "EUVD-2026-86800", "enisaUuid": "18d161de-a516-37ab-af78-5542016cdb13", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/amd_node: Fix PCI device reference counting in amd_smn_init()\n\nThe local \"root\" pointer is a temporary variable used during the device\nsearch. Therefore, refcount related to the search iterators should be cleaned\nup after the search is complete.\n\nUse the __free() cleanup macro to ensure the refcount is decremented when the\ntemporary pointer goes out of scope.\n\nAdditionally, increment the refcount when caching a root pointer. This ensures\nthe in-use refcount is separate from the temporary search refcounting.\n\nFinally, drop the redundant \"root = NULL\" before the second search loop. The\npci_get_class() iterator always decrements the refcount of its \"from\"\nargument, so the first loop can only fall through with \"root\" already NULL.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84e3a71d11d8593c127b468d75b2653af5074f81", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa2a4277ad42fd8f918c6dc652473946a253f7b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/27600805e62f800bacf990354632eae4e487d34c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vfm8-xw8f-q53w", "CVE-2026-97946"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "12aa26d3-65de-3a39-bb6d-04f928ccd8c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "3bedd77f-3c22-3b45-a6ca-c6aefaf1ef7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "54732b74-7e49-32ed-82bf-41c40e49ca8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "84f8fa5b-5456-3215-b069-436da053cb75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4b61d9c2e496b5f0a10e29e355a1465c8738bb <84e3a71d11d8593c127b468d75b2653af5074f81"}, {"id": "8518d28f-970f-31b0-b591-eae8b63c1be3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "896176e3-c9f9-30e1-bc28-08c8cb60a4ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c4ad899a33198ab6335732c769835d035e66894a"}, {"id": "8f38acbe-4095-34f6-9d99-4c420700fd5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17.8 <6.18"}, {"id": "a04fe785-1cb7-3343-9149-75de38445d87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4b61d9c2e496b5f0a10e29e355a1465c8738bb <aa2a4277ad42fd8f918c6dc652473946a253f7b0"}, {"id": "d8357449-895c-33af-8da1-1b888e3c03e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4b61d9c2e496b5f0a10e29e355a1465c8738bb <27600805e62f800bacf990354632eae4e487d34c"}, {"id": "f4caa09b-fb34-3362-9fcf-3abc3d8af5e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f5133961-65b9-3f61-9824-353f1e27f23e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}